WEBVTT

00:00:09.227 --> 00:00:10.467
I'm so sorry.

00:00:10.547 --> 00:00:12.467
(STAMMERS) It was an accident.

00:00:13.187 --> 00:00:14.867
What? This?

00:00:14.987 --> 00:00:18.627
My one souvenir
from a lifetime of Scaring?

00:00:19.387 --> 00:00:22.027
Accidents happen, don't they.

00:00:22.627 --> 00:00:25.507
The important thing is no one got hurt.

00:00:26.907 --> 00:00:28.867
You're taking this remarkably well.

00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:31.667
Now, let's continue the exams.

00:00:32.307 --> 00:00:34.787
Mr. Wazowski, I'm a five-year-old girl

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:36.827
on a farm in Kansas afraid of lightning.

00:00:37.147 --> 00:00:38.547
Which Scare do you use?

00:00:39.747 --> 00:00:41.427
Shouldn't I go up on the...

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.747
Which Scare do you use?

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:47.187
That is a Shadow Approach
with a Crackle Holler.

00:00:47.387 --> 00:00:48.387
Demonstrate.

00:00:49.227 --> 00:00:50.387
(INHALES)

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.467
-Stop. Thank you.
-But I didn't get to...

00:00:52.547 --> 00:00:53.987
I've seen enough.

00:00:55.227 --> 00:00:56.547
I'm a seven-year-old boy...

00:00:56.867 --> 00:00:58.267
(ROARS LOUDLY)

00:00:59.387 --> 00:01:00.547
I wasn't finished.

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.707
I don't need to know
any of that stuff to scare.

00:01:03.427 --> 00:01:05.907
That "stuff" would've informed you

00:01:05.987 --> 00:01:08.667
that this particular child
is afraid of snakes.

00:01:09.187 --> 00:01:12.107
So a roar wouldn't make him scream,
it would make him cry,

00:01:12.187 --> 00:01:15.027
alerting his parents,
exposing the monster world,

00:01:15.107 --> 00:01:16.707
destroying life as we know it,

00:01:16.787 --> 00:01:18.547
and of course we can't have that.

00:01:18.627 --> 00:01:20.787
So I'm afraid I cannot
recommend that you continue

00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:23.387
in the Scaring program. Good day.

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:25.587
Wait, what? But I'm a Sullivan.

00:01:26.227 --> 00:01:28.347
Well then, I'm sure your family

00:01:28.427 --> 00:01:30.387
will be very disappointed.

00:01:31.587 --> 00:01:32.587
(FOOTSTEPS RETREATING)

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:35.307
(STUDENTS MURMURING)

00:01:40.987 --> 00:01:42.227
(GRUNTS)

00:01:42.307 --> 00:01:43.747
(MURMURING CONTINUES)

00:01:45.587 --> 00:01:49.107
And, Mr. Wazowski,
what you lack is something

00:01:49.187 --> 00:01:50.787
that cannot be taught.

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:53.787
You're not scary.

00:01:56.107 --> 00:01:58.987
You will not be continuing
in the Scaring program.

00:02:00.307 --> 00:02:02.907
Please. Let me try the simulator.
I'll surprise you.

00:02:03.627 --> 00:02:07.427
Surprise me? I doubt that very much.

00:02:18.147 --> 00:02:19.427
(WIND WHOOSHING)

00:02:19.507 --> 00:02:20.707
SCREAM-CAN PROFESSOR:
Welcome back.

00:02:21.947 --> 00:02:24.547
I hope everyone had a pleasant break.

00:02:25.907 --> 00:02:30.267
Some say that a career
as a scream-can designer is boring,

00:02:30.347 --> 00:02:35.107
unchallenging, a waste
of a monster's potential.

00:02:36.467 --> 00:02:37.747
(INHALES DEEPLY)

00:02:37.827 --> 00:02:40.867
Open your textbooks to chapter three.

00:02:40.947 --> 00:02:43.867
We will now plunge into the rich history

00:02:44.147 --> 00:02:46.387
-of scream-can design.
-(SQUEAKS)

00:02:48.227 --> 00:02:49.987
(STUDENTS CHATTERING
INDISTINCTLY)

00:03:17.107 --> 00:03:18.467
(GRUNTS)

00:03:30.427 --> 00:03:31.667
(CHUCKLES)

00:03:32.347 --> 00:03:33.547
Out of my way!

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:36.587
Coming through! Oh, sorry. Ha-ha!

00:03:37.147 --> 00:03:41.147
Welcome to this year's
Greek Scare Games kickoff.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.907
-The Scare Games! Yeah!
-(MARCHING BAND PLAYING)

00:03:44.987 --> 00:03:47.067
-(FEEDBACK)
-Okay, relax.

00:03:47.147 --> 00:03:51.187
We have a special guest,
the founder of the games,

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:53.507
Dean Hardscrabble.

00:03:53.587 --> 00:03:54.707
(CROWD CHEERING)

00:03:55.587 --> 00:03:56.547
Good afternoon.

00:03:57.427 --> 00:04:00.187
As a student, I created these games

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:01.947
as a friendly competition,

00:04:02.627 --> 00:04:04.667
but be prepared.

00:04:04.747 --> 00:04:06.187
To take home the trophy,

00:04:06.307 --> 00:04:09.667
you must be the most fearsome
monsters on campus.

00:04:10.027 --> 00:04:11.027
(RORS CHUCKLING)

00:04:11.107 --> 00:04:14.827
So good luck,
and may the best monsters win.

00:04:14.907 --> 00:04:16.187
-(CROWD CHEERING)
-All right, everybody.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:18.547
We're closing down sign-ups,
so we'll see you all...

00:04:18.627 --> 00:04:19.627
MIKE: Wait!

00:04:21.707 --> 00:04:22.947
I'm signing up!

00:04:23.387 --> 00:04:24.547
(CROWD LAUGHING)

00:04:24.867 --> 00:04:26.267
What?

00:04:28.107 --> 00:04:29.987
Uh... You have to be
in a fraternity to compete.

00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:33.667
Behold the next winning fraternity
of the Scare Games,

00:04:33.747 --> 00:04:38.427
the brothers, my brothers,
of Oozma Kappa!

00:04:40.147 --> 00:04:41.547
Hi.

00:04:41.627 --> 00:04:42.707
(HISSING)

00:04:43.507 --> 00:04:45.627
Mr. Wazowski, what are you doing?

00:04:45.707 --> 00:04:48.307
You just said the winners are the most
fearsome monsters on campus.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:50.787
If I win, it means
you kicked out the best Scarer

00:04:51.107 --> 00:04:52.587
in the whole school.

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:53.787
That won't happen.

00:04:54.387 --> 00:04:55.787
How about a little wager?

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:59.307
If I win, you let me back
in the Scaring program.

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:00.467
(SCOFFS)

00:05:01.547 --> 00:05:03.307
And what would that prove?

00:05:03.987 --> 00:05:05.147
That you were wrong.

00:05:05.787 --> 00:05:07.147
(ALL GASP)

00:05:09.027 --> 00:05:10.227
Very well.

00:05:10.387 --> 00:05:13.867
If you win, I will let your entire team

00:05:13.947 --> 00:05:15.467
into the Scare program.

